       POSIX.1 requires that an implementation allow at least AATTEEXXIITT__MMAAXX  (32)
       such  functions to be registered.  The actual limit supported by an im‐
       plementation can be obtained using ssyyssccoonnff(3).

       When a child process is created via ffoorrkk(2), it inherits copies of  its
       parent’s  registrations.   Upon a successful call to one of the eexxeecc(3)
       functions, all registrations are removed.

